exports[`FoldingRenderer > matches the DOM snapshot of a fixed item 1`] = `"<section class="hb-render folding svelte-akthb0"><p class="stem svelte-akthb0">A square sheet of paper is folded as shown, then a hole is punched through every layer. Which option shows the sheet when it is unfolded?</p> <div class="figure" role="group" aria-label="How the sheet is folded and punched"><ol class="hb-sr-only"><li>The sheet is a square with a 4 by 4 grid of places for holes. Rows are numbered 1 to 4 from the top, and columns 1 to 4 from the left.</li> <li>Step 1: the sheet is folded in half along its vertical centre line; the left half is folded over onto the right half.</li><li>Step 2: the folded paper is folded in half along its horizontal centre line; the top half is folded over onto the bottom half.</li><li>Step 3: the folded paper is folded in half along its horizontal centre line; the bottom half is folded over onto the top half.</li><!----> <li>Then a hole is punched through every layer at row 3, column 4 of the sheet.</li></ol> <div class="panels svelte-akthb0" aria-hidden="true"><figure class="panel svelte-akthb0"><svg class="paper svelte-akthb0" focusable="false" viewBox="-1.2 -1.2 10.4 10.4"><defs><pattern patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse" width="0.8" height="0.8" patternTransform="rotate(45)" id="c1-hatch-0"><line class="hatch svelte-akthb0" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="0.8"></line></pattern></defs><!----><polygon class="sheet svelte-akthb0" points="0,0 8,0 8,8 0,8"></polygon><polygon class="moving svelte-akthb0" points="0,0 4,0 4,8 0,8" fill="url(#c1-hatch-0)"></polygon><line class="fold svelte-akthb0" x1="4" y1="0" x2="4" y2="8"></line><path class="arrow svelte-akthb0" d="M 2 4 Q 4 2.2 5.33 3.4"></path><polygon class="head svelte-akthb0" points="6,4 4.97,3.8 5.69,3"></polygon></svg> <figcaption class="svelte-akthb0">Fold 1</figcaption></figure><figure class="panel svelte-akthb0"><svg class="paper svelte-akthb0" focusable="false" viewBox="-1.2 -1.2 10.4 10.4"><defs><patter